  "notes": "Each of Greene's 42 precincts elects one male and one female Republican County Committee member (per the county's candidate listing). The county results site reports each precinct as one 'vote for 2' contest, lists only ballot candidates, and publishes no write-in totals; it does not show the candidates' sex. Status rules: no ballot candidate = 'empty_no_filer' (write-ins could have won but are not published); top vote-getter = 'filled'; where two or more candidates ran, the second seat is 'unknown' because the results do not show whether the runner-up is eligible for the other-sex seat (18 precincts). Results and candidate listing agree on which 25 precincts had candidates. Seats are labeled 'Member' because the results do not distinguish them. Appointments after the primary are not reflected."
